# Patterns and boundaries

- Prefer a feature-service method over a new abstraction. Add a type, interface, or provider only for a real external boundary or two interchangeable implementations.
- Use Strategy for approved external ports (`PaymentGateway`, `SmsSender`, `Storage`). Use a factory only in composition/configuration to choose one adapter. Do not add a factory for entities, DTOs, or one implementation.
- Nest providers are singleton by default. Do not create manual `static getInstance()` singletons or a service locator.
- Use an in-process observer/event only for non-critical post-commit work. Required writes remain explicit service calls in the same transaction; do not add a generic event bus or CQRS layer.
- Keep Socket.IO limited to the documented order-status monitoring channel. It is not a command transport or a replacement for REST.
